Z||000000||hugh||09-09-2001||08:54 AM||||Last night I was coming home from Fogglethorpe's house when a new BMW blew by me on the right at a light going about 60.I didn't see him coming and he scared the hell out of me.At the next light (red) he again got into the right lane in order to beat the other cars stopped at the light.When the light changed he was off like a shot,so was I.When we cleared the cars in the left lane I stepped on it and blew by him in the left lane enough to get well in front of him when it narrowed to one lane.Then I drove at just below the speed limit.When it was clear to pass he did and I gave him a one finger salute.Let me say,I was never on the wrong side of the road and I didn't need to go over 55 in a 45 MPH limit area.I just got there one hell of a lot faster than he could!By the way,this was in my Grand National. ||||reg||10
Z||000001||fiero56||09-09-2001||09:23 AM||||If I had been the bimmer I'd have been giving you the 'salute'.<P>Damn pisses me off when people purosefully blast in front of me before a road narrows to 2 lanes, only to go slower than the speed limit.<P>Depends on what model it was. Those little 318s and such are pretty slow, but I'd like to see your G/N against an M5 or similar.||||reg||1
Z||000002||hugh||09-09-2001||09:30 AM||||Does it piss you off to have somebody blast by you 100 feet before their lane ends at twice your speed? It scared the hell out of me.I've run 115 at a traction limited 12.20.Since then I've made a few changes and the car should be capable of 117/118 at near mid 11's.If they can do that more power to them.||||reg||1
