Z||000026||LZeitgeist||09-09-2001||08:04 PM||||O.K., hugh - here's your answer.<P>Given the same set of circumstances, here's what I would have done. <P>NOTHING. <P>The dude didn't do anything *to* you! If asked, he probably couldn't have even told you what kinds of cars were in the line of traffic he just passed. <P>He was driving in a possibly unsafe manner for questionable reasons, but he was going through open lanes where there was no traffic. Speeding, yes. Road raging? Who knows - but my first guess would be that since there was no traffic in his way, he had no reason to be 'raging'. <P>However, you altered the parameters of the situation to make it a larger problem for all involved. And for what? So you could feel like a 'big man', proving to him that you could be an even BIGGER danger to society that HE was. Yup, way to go, slugger. Guess you showed him. <P>Given the same circumstances, I would have recovered from being startled as he went by, probably called him an a$$hole (to myself, since he's obviously out of hearing range), and gone about my merry way. <P>Just as you should have done. <P>Let a$$holes be a$$holes. Doesn't mean you have to join them.||||reg||1
