Z||000033||hugh||09-10-2001||01:04 AM||||When I started this thread,I had no idea what I was letting myself in for.I can say I have read about road rage and seen the results of it on television,but I never thought of myself as doing it.When you react to someone else's actions in any way it is road rage.What I did in no way endangered anyone else,but it was in fact road rage.I didn't expect the reactions I got from some of the people on this forum.I didn't want a pat on the back or to hear nice kill(I don't even like that term),but I didn't expect to hear all this righteous indignation about what is wrong with what I did.It seems it's time to coin a new word just for the internet,how about net rage.That would be reacting to what someone else has written on the net.Some of you practice it on here by attacking anyone that makes a statement that leaves an opening for it.I know that I will be subject to it again for this post but I am at the point where I could care less about what some of you think or say.For an analogy,I see some of you as a pack of predators surrounding a weakened prey waiting for an opening.<P>Fiero56 how aboutBlack/White<BR>                 Day/Night<BR>                 Salt/Pepper<BR>What I mean is no matter what I say you will come back with a different(read opposite) point of view. <BR>Formula  Your original response was real class.You can still stick that finger.<BR>LZeitgeist at this point in time I would say that you are the best at net rage,but you have had practice,since I am not the first one on this forum to be subjected to it.<BR>Johnnyk  Every time you get called on your stupid comments you call it a joke.I personally am tired of you.<BR>Mach10 No offense but you suck.What does that mean?<BR>One more thing,I am not mad,or upset,just tired of the argueing.<BR>OK people,fire at will. ||||reg||1
